content.text:
{
  "expand": "renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations",
  "id": "3154344",
  "self": "https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/9dfc393f-ac2d-4cef-8b1c-0657da26067f/rest/api/3/issue/3154344",
  "key": "QP-2862",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "[4.5] Basic lane in Authenticate for Xsolla-issued publisher keys",
    "description": "**Plan task 4.5** · Depends on: 4.2, 4.3, plan tasks 1.4 and 3.2 · Blocks: 4.6, 5.1, 6.1\n\nScope is route-carried, never credential-derived. Partly forced — `project_id` is unrecoverable from a Basic credential, whose username half is the merchant ID — and partly chosen: a body-supplied scope can be varied by the caller, letting them influence which authorization question is asked about their own request.\n\nThe **vendor call is the authorization boundary**. The local lookup supplies the internal account ID and rejects un-onboarded projects as defence in depth.\n\n* \\[ \\] Replace plan task 3.1's `Basic` placeholder: parse `Basic base64(merchant_ID:api_key)`, rejecting malformed input as 401 without logging the secret.\n* \\[ \\] Require `project_id` from the route. A Basic credential on a route without it is unresolvable by construction — reject rather than paper over.\n* \\[ \\] Local lookup first (4.2), then the ownership cross-check against `accounts.xsolla_merchant_id`.\n* \\[ \\] Vendor validation (4.3) after the local checks pass. Uncached, so every admitted request round-trips to Xsolla.\n* \\[ \\] Resolve the service identity by **home scope plus discriminator**, not a stored vendor ref: for a project-level key, the Xsolla-credential service identity homed at the resolved account; for a company-level key, the one homed at that account's workspace. `GetXsollaByHomeScope` is a single-row read thanks to the partial unique index.\n* \\[ \\] Handle the case where a merchant has **both** a company-level and a project-level Xsolla service identity, and document the resolution order. Project-level first is the narrower grant and the safer default.\n* \\[ \\] Produce `Principal{Kind: KindService, Source: \"publisher\", ...}` with the home scope from the service identity.\n* \\[ \\] Code comment recording the lane asymmetry: machines derive the home scope from the credential, humans from route plus access list. Same `Principal` downstream, but this must be visible in code or it will be misread.\n* \\[ \\] End-to-end tests: project key on its own project → author on the mapped account; company key on any owned project → capabilities via the workspace cascade; company key on a foreign project → 404; unmapped project → 404 with no vendor call.\n\n",
    "assignee": null,
    "status": {
      "self": "https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/9dfc393f-ac2d-4cef-8b1c-0657da26067f/rest/api/3/status/18738",
      "description": "",
      "iconUrl": "https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/9dfc393f-ac2d-4cef-8b1c-0657da26067f/",
      "name": "К выполнению",
      "id": "18738",
      "statusCategory": {
        "self": "https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/9dfc393f-ac2d-4cef-8b1c-0657da26067f/rest/api/3/statuscategory/2",
        "id": 2,
        "key": "new",
        "colorName": "blue-gray",
        "name": "К выполнению"
      }
    }
  }
}

